                <pb facs="0783" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg649"/>

                <head>No. 470.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pendleton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 19,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 341.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Coleman’s No. 635, of the 2d instant, and to approve his transmission, through
                    the proper channel, of the appeal to the Prussian minister of finance regarding
                    the income tax recently assessed on the American citizen S. R. Honey by the
                    government authorities at Frankfort.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
